# Comprehensive Project Prompt: Inclusive Learning Management System (ILS)

Create a complete **Inclusive Learning Management System (ILS)** - a fully accessible educational platform designed for students with disabilities. This should be a production-ready LMS with comprehensive accessibility features, multi-role support, and modern UI.

## Core Requirements

### 1. Database Schema & Setup
Create a complete Supabase database with the following tables and relationships:

**Users & Profiles:**
- `profiles` table with: id, user_id (FK to auth.users), first_name, last_name, role, parent_email, disabilities (array), school_name, created_at, updated_at
- `email_invitations` table with: id, email, role, invited_by, token, used, expires_at, additional_data (JSON)

**Educational Structure:**
- `schools` table with: id, name, principal_id, created_at, updated_at
- `classes` table with: id, name, description, school_id, teacher_id, enrollment_code, created_at, updated_at
- `subjects` table with: id, name, description, class_id, created_at, updated_at
- `student_enrollments` table with: id, student_id, class_id, enrolled_at

**Content & Assessments:**
- `lessons` table with: id, title, description, content, subject_id, lesson_order, created_at, updated_at
- `assignments` table with: id, title, description, subject_id, due_date, max_score, max_attempts, allowed_file_types (array), created_at, updated_at
- `assignment_submissions` table with: id, assignment_id, student_id, submission_text, file_path, score, feedback, attempt_number, submitted_at, graded_by, graded_at
- `quizzes` table with: id, title, description, subject_id, questions (JSON), time_limit, max_attempts, max_score, created_at, updated_at
- `quiz_attempts` table with: id, quiz_id, student_id, answers (JSON), score, attempt_number, completed_at, created_at

**Materials & Videos:**
- `materials` table with: id, title, description, file_path, file_type, lesson_id, subject_id, uploaded_by, created_at
- `video_materials` table with: id, title, description, file_path, thumbnail_path, transcript_text, captions_path, audio_description_path, sign_language_video_path, duration, resolution, video_format, file_size, category, difficulty_level, tags (array), lesson_id, subject_id, uploaded_by, created_at, updated_at
- `video_progress` table with: id, video_id, student_id, progress_seconds, completed, last_watched

**Notifications:**
- `notifications` table with: id, user_id, title, message, type, read, created_at

### 2. Authentication & User Management
Implement complete authentication system with:
- **Role-based access:** principal, teacher, student, parent
- **Email invitation system:** Send password setup emails instead of creating passwords directly
- **Forgot password functionality:** Complete email reset flow
- **Invitation acceptance flow:** Handle invitation tokens and account setup
- **Parent linking:** Automatically invite parents when student email is added

### 3. Row Level Security (RLS) Policies
Implement comprehensive RLS policies:
- Principals can manage everything in their domain
- Teachers can manage their classes, subjects, assignments, and students
- Students can only access their enrolled content and submit work
- Parents can view their children's progress
- Public video access for guest users
- Proper security definer functions to avoid infinite recursion

### 4. User Interfaces & Dashboards

**Dashboard System:**
Create role-specific dashboards with:

**Principal Dashboard:**
- School overview with teacher/student/class statistics
- Teacher and class management
- System-wide reports and analytics
- Notification management
- User invitation system

**Teacher Dashboard:**
- Class and subject management with dropdown showing ALL available classes
- Assignment and quiz creation/grading
- Student management with email invitation system
- Student progress tracking and reports
- Parent email management for students

**Student Dashboard:**
- Enrolled classes and subjects overview
- Assignment submissions and grades
- Quiz taking interface
- Video learning progress
- Accessibility preferences

**Parent Dashboard:**
- Child progress monitoring
- Assignment and grade tracking
- Teacher communication
- Event calendar
- Accessibility feature usage tracking

### 5. Comprehensive Accessibility Features

**Core Accessibility:**
- Full keyboard navigation support
- Screen reader compatibility (ARIA labels, semantic HTML)
- High contrast mode toggle
- Font size adjustment (small, medium, large, extra-large)
- Text-to-Speech (TTS) system with voice controls
- Visual alerts and announcements
- Skip navigation links
- Focus management

**TTS Implementation:**
- Complete TTS context with voice selection
- TTS buttons on all content
- Keyboard shortcuts (T key to read content)
- Voice speed controls
- Screen reader announcements for all actions

**Video Accessibility:**
- Closed captions and transcripts
- Audio descriptions
- Sign language video overlays
- Keyboard controls (space, arrows, M, C, F keys)
- Progress tracking and bookmarks
- Customizable playback speeds

